  "note": "One decision table for both harness guards. rule is the rule that must block the call, or empty when the call is allowed. situation names the PATH the hook runs with: fd-rg (fd and rg installed), rg (only rg), fd (only fd) or none. A grep is blocked only while rg is on PATH, and a find rule names fd or, without fd, the built-in tool. hooks/claude/toolguard_test.py runs every case through the real Claude hooks; TestCtxReminderSharedToolguardCases in tool runs the same file through the pi extension and compares blocked vs allowed and the rule name only. builtinCases is the second table: pi's own grep and find tools (Claude has no built-in search rules). tool is harness-neutral (content-search for pi grep, file-search for pi find), rule.pi is the rule that must block (empty for allowed), and path names the target directory; an absolute path outside the repository must be allowed. The built-in grep is blocked while rg is on PATH, the built-in find while fd is.",
